{#
	ACF layout: media_full — the project screenshot on work-single.

	Alt text comes from the media library's own field. An image with no alt
	renders alt="" and is announced as decorative, which is correct for a
	screenshot that the surrounding copy already describes — but wrong for
	anything carrying information, so fill it in.
#}

{#
	The field returns an ACF **array**, not a Timber Image, so `src()` and
	`srcset` are not available on it — calling them silently produced `src=""`.
	It went unnoticed because no seeded row ever had an image in it. Read the
	array the same way `ui/section-background.twig` does: `url`, `ID`, `width`,
	`height`, and the srcset from WordPress itself.
#}

{% if section.image.url %}
	{% set srcset = function('wp_get_attachment_image_srcset', section.image.ID, 'large') %}

	<section class="media-full">
		<div class="{{ section.width == 'narrow' ? 'container-narrow' : 'container' }}">
			<figure class="media-full__figure">
				<img
					src="{{ section.image.url }}"
					{% if srcset %}srcset="{{ srcset }}"{% endif %}
					sizes="{{ section.width == 'narrow' ? '(min-width: 47.5rem) 760px, 100vw' : '(min-width: 75rem) 1200px, 100vw' }}"
					alt="{{ section.image.alt }}"
					width="{{ section.image.width }}"
					height="{{ section.image.height }}"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
				>

				{% if section.caption %}
					<figcaption class="media-full__caption">{{ section.caption }}</figcaption>
				{% endif %}
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>
{% endif %}
